{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games","id":399097,"title":"\"Big Five\" crossover games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-09T11:44:04-08:00","id":399097,"title":"\"Big Five\" crossover games","content":"Has anyone done a game with the &quot;big five,&quot; as in have a Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Changeling and Wraith in one group? If so, how did it work out? What was the overall plot? Were Mages overpowered? Were Werewolves overpowered? Was different game mechanics a major problem? What about the conflicting cosmology of the games? <br /> <br /> And more importantly what was the explanation for how they all came together? Been thinking about perhaps trying to bring the idea to my table and was hoping for some perspectives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:04:41-08:00","id":399127,"title":"","content":"I have sort of it was more going of a big 7 so add HTR and demon in there. We originally had two mages a hunter and a risen wraith but the last two left then we got two demons. It ran pretty good. The overall plot was a small town where nothing really happens has something BIG happen and it's up to the players to work with the various supernatural powers to deal with it. The different mechanics were not an issue save for some of my unfamiliarity some mage stuff.<br /> <br /> The mages were overpowered unless they were dealing with a fellow mage or this one vampire which had an ability that gave him extra dodge dice which they managed to beat with luck, but the game was more focused on the story and they weren't OP enough that it broke the game or the story line and everything that I wanted to happen, happened in some manner. <br /> <br /> How the group got together was that each of the characters had a reason to go after the big bad, The Hunter's girlfriend was killed by the big bad and the big bad was also responsible for his imbuing, the Mage's have a truce with the local Cam's who got something important stolen from them by the big bad and so to keep the peace they wanted to get the stolen item back, also their chantry didn't really have much for them to do a lot so this gave them something to do and test their magic out on. The wraith was supposed to infiltrate the local camps and work for them so that's how he would get involved, and the demons got information that some world changing event was going to happen that was linked to the big bad so they were hoping to try and stop it or find out what it was. <br /> <br /> It also helped helped the at all the players and myself were good friends and have been in many games together so we have a strong trust and know that were not going to be trying to screwing each other over. <br /> <br /> I was also in a crossover game that allowed for any splat so long as it fit the story and it worked well. We had 4 vamps 1 werewolf and 2 Hunter side characters.<br /> Save for myself and the sheriff everyone was playing a character new to the supernatural world or out of the loop so no one really had any prejudices and the local vampires and werewolf's had a<br /> truce were &quot;you stay out of our area, and we'll stay out of yours&quot; deal unless shit hit the fan and they had to temporally pull resources. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:21:14-08:00","id":399170,"title":"","content":"I personally think crossover does nothing more than muddy the themes of the composite games and lead to horrid power differences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:48:44-08:00","id":399197,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">My opinion:<br /> The Big Three (Werewolf, Mage, and Vampire) work well enough together. Even then, I do some slight (or major) system tweaks to make things jive a smidge smoother. Wraith is really awkward or really easy, depending on the player and character. So I don't have to deal with the headaches of including Risen (which, in my mind, is another half-splat) I strongly encourage Embody 4. Changeling is a huge pain. I incorporated CtD in a crossover game for only one Chronicle. It worked, but I stole mercilessly from <i>Land of Eight Million Dreams</i> and added some odd alterations. If I had to do it over again, I'd use DtF with a &quot;goblin mod.&quot;<br /> <br /> The following are some of the tweaks that I use:<br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Use the magic system for DA: Mage. It just meshes better with crossover\u2019d systems.<br /> <br /> Werewolves work well enough with minimal finagling, except for one tiny thing: Crinos. Werewolves in these games can only be in Crinos for [Perm. Rage] turns. I think WtF does something similar.<br /> <br /> Vampires and Sunlight. I mess with this a great deal in Crossover games. It kills the flow of the story when one the characters can\u2019t function AT ALL for half the day.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">In Crossover Games (only): Vampires can spend a Blood Point at sunrise to take soakable Bashing dice (not levels) from Sunlight. They have to cover up (hats, ponchos, long sleeves, etc.) but they can still do stuff. They just have to do it carefully. To balance this out, vampires (regardless of the time) soak other damage like a human (bullets do lethal, no halving Bashing, etc.). Also, no sun screen. For no reason other than it seems dangerously close to that threshold of absurdity.</span><br /> <br /> While some of these are a little odd, they work well enough for me. It helps curb random RAW-lawyers that may get incorporated into the troupe and helps me set the proper tone for game expectations. <br /> <br /> And now, the obligatory \u201cYMMV.\u201d</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T18:27:55-08:00","id":399660,"title":"","content":"I tend to dislike mixed PC groups, but a few here or there can work well. A single mage with a pack of werewolves can work. Vampires and Mages of certain types can work. Wraiths and Mages of certain types can work very well. Changelings are a pain in the ass.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> When mixing Vampires...<br /> <br /> Instead of neutering the sunlight thing for Vampires, allow them to create a single ghoul with character creation. It will be a sort of second-skin for them. This will be their daylight character. They might have more ghouls, but this one is the one they PC.<br /> <br /> In the past this solution has allowed me to keep some dark and cursed themes on the Vampire while giving them access to Mage time frames too. It does give them an advantage, but less than (I think) being day walkers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T06:50:15-08:00","id":400267,"title":"","content":"I ran a very successful Vampire/Werewolf/Changeling crossover once. It still holds the record as one of my longest running chronicles.<br /> <br /> That said, I do prefer single game lines for the PCs. I'll still mine the other games for antagonists, but they'll be presented through the lens of whatever game the PCs are from. For example, I'm running a Mage chronicle right now where the characters have found themselves neck deep in vampire politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T07:44:22-08:00","id":400309,"title":"","content":"Current Group:<br /> <br /> 1 Ravnos, 1 Kiasyd, 1 Scourge, 1 Anansi, 1 Imbued Visionary, 1 Western Equivalent of a Wan Kuei(I just call em Revenants and be damned to the previous usage)<br /> <br /> Imbued player had been playing a Risen earlier in the campaign,<br /> <br /> Fun Being Had: LOTS!<br /> <br /> I had to adapt the rules a lot though, spend a lot of time trying to get the various settings to cohere in the same world, that took about a year, which i had time for since i was in hospital awaiting a back op and recovering after.<br /> <br /> I used Vampire Revised as the base, and ensured all the splats fit into that mold, with Virtues and a Path rating. Had to also ensure that there were crossover friendly rules, and always allow a save roll, even if the power doesnt have one. The homebrew rules document is...large... but my players are enthusiastic.<br /> <br /> So far so good,<br /> <br /> its been exhausting, lots of setting elements have had to be finessed, but i daresay it resembles the World Of Darkness, just through a Mirror Darkly.<br /> <br /> Also Mages are broken so they got vetoed and made NPC only, and only one in a million, the majority of the spellslinger organizations are composed of sorcerers instead, with Magi as the almost mythical ans reclusive leadership for the most part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T08:01:06-08:00","id":400318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games?p=400309#post400309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Current Group:<br /> <br /> 1 Ravnos, 1 Kiasyd, 1 Scourge, 1 Anansi, 1 Imbued Visionary, 1 Western Equivalent of a Wan Kuei(I just call em Revenants and be damned to the previous usage)<br /> <br /> Imbued player had been playing a Risen earlier in the campaign,<br /> <br /> Fun Being Had: LOTS!<br /> <br /> I had to adapt the rules a lot though, spend a lot of time trying to get the various settings to cohere in the same world, that took about a year, which i had time for since i was in hospital awaiting a back op and recovering after.<br /> <br /> I used Vampire Revised as the base, and ensured all the splats fit into that mold, with Virtues and a Path rating. Had to also ensure that there were crossover friendly rules, and always allow a save roll, even if the power doesnt have one. The homebrew rules document is...large... but my players are enthusiastic.<br /> <br /> So far so good,<br /> <br /> its been exhausting, lots of setting elements have had to be finessed, but i daresay it resembles the World Of Darkness, just through a Mirror Darkly.<br /> <br /> Also Mages are broken so they got vetoed and made NPC only, and only one in a million, the majority of the spellslinger organizations are composed of sorcerers instead, with Magi as the almost mythical ans reclusive leadership for the most part.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I am jealous. I have always wanted to play an Ananasi, but never had a chance.<br /> <br /> And on an off-note, I can agree with you about Mages. I try to keep a fully blended crossover Universe (which I also keep continuous in that it has been the setting for basically all of my games), but blending Mages into other PC groups can be difficult. It requires a lot of maturity from the player, to keep with the themes of the story instead of just brute-force magicking his way through it.<br /> <br /> If I were running a mixed PC group for players I did not know well enough to insult harshly (in a loving way!), I might agree with your idea of keeping Mages out of the picture.<br /> <br /> Also - quick note - 1 in 1,000,000 is far too common. 1 in 5 million minimum. One in a million is still 7200 Awakened world-wide. That is a massive number, especially in a game without Mage PCs. 1 in 5 mill is 1440 Mages worldwide, which is still pretty influential. 1 in 10 million would be 720 Mages world-wide, which now makes them super rare and the chance of any of them influencing your PC is very low.<br /> <br /> That probably doesn't even matter, I am just being a nerd this morning. :-P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T11:56:35-08:00","id":400598,"title":"","content":"The last LARP I was in was a free for all. Mostly Vampires, but from all the obscure Bloodlines (Lamia, Kiyasid, True Brujah, etc), random assortments of shape-changers (Ceilican, Simba, Anasazi), 3 mages (two Trad one Orphan), and a Chulichuan (if I remember correctly).<br /> <br /> The big thing I remember from it is that there are time to ignore the cosmology and time to embrace it. Time to play loose with the rules and times to tighten them like a noose.<br /> <br /> As long as people are having fun and the internal logic and flow of the game remains the same, you just have to run with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T07:20:29-08:00","id":401826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games#post399097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone done a game with the &quot;big five,&quot; as in have a Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Changeling and Wraith in one group? If so, how did it work out? What was the overall plot? Were Mages overpowered? Were Werewolves overpowered? Was different game mechanics a major problem? What about the conflicting cosmology of the games?<br /> <br /> And more importantly what was the explanation for how they all came together? Been thinking about perhaps trying to bring the idea to my table and was hoping for some perspectives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love Mage but mages will break other games. Use sorcerers instead","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T07:52:45-08:00","id":401898,"title":"","content":"Regarding why the group exists, i had them all working for Samael, or Lucifer as he is also known, living in LA guarding the vampire parents of the Last Daughter of Eve. The child will inherit the power and be the avatar of Lilith on Earth during the Apocalypse. So the story started set in 1991, with the group working for their patrons, senior exemplars of their kind who had allied with Samael at some point in the past. When their patrons were killed they took over the duties of their seniors, and when the parents were killed they took over raising little Alia.<br /> <br /> The game is a mix of the characters pursuing their own interests, and protecting the child and LA from incursions into by other interested parties, including Lilith's agents on Earth, who are understandably concerned about getting their Mother's avatar back.<br /> <br /> The timeline progresses 5 years between every season, and each season a new problem rears its head that the group as a whole need to deal with.<br /> <br /> Samael is a good-ish guy, the biggest guns have concrete reasons not to throwdown till the night of the Apocalypse, and the players each have reasons for seeing Samael's will be done, from compassion for the parents and the child, to pure self interest(Raising a God, how is that not beneficial?).<br /> <br /> The setting has a lot of changes, minor and major to make it all fit, including an actual Hell for the dead, ala Yomi in the East, and Hell-lords who rule it, and so on.<br /> <br /> Regarding the number of Mages, while 1 in a million leads to several thousand mages, most of them leave the Earth behind and go beyond the gauntlet for a variety of reasons. The single largest block of Magi, the Technocracy are involved in protecting the borders of the Universe from the Outsiders, creatures from the previous Universe desperate to come into the new Universe.(Hello Dresden-verse Meets Exalted. The Outsiders are the remnants of the Exalted-verse Primordial Demon Hordes) With that war ongoing the Technos throw as many Mages as they can spare at that war, and the Traditions, despite their enmity often find themselves performing similar duties. That leaves a minority of mages on Earth, from either the Traditions, the Technocracy, or from Orphan groups to play around on Earth. Mages also just find the world beyond the Gauntlet more congenial as there is no Paradox, and Mages can achieve godlike acts in the Umbra or the Underworld.<br /> <br /> It's not that the Outsider War is the single most important game, but it keeps the Magi occupied, while other factions run around in the shadows of the WoD, awaiting the Apocalypse and advancing their plans. The Outsider War also blinds the Mages to just how damn dangerous the War between the Wyrm, the Weaver and the Wyld actually is. By ignoring that conflict the Mages may save the Universe just to see the Wyrm destroy everything, the Weaver freeze everything to Stasis, or the Wyld unmake meaning altogether.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, thats part of the setting adjustments i had to make. Its been fun so far.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T09:33:26-08:00","id":401969,"title":"","content":"It is a pain in the ass when running a Crossover game period. All the variants in the game? Different creatures are way more powerful than others like the Garou who are the strongest starting in the game. The Crossover rules are a nightmare. <br /> <br /> I remember Jess Hening and Justin Anchilli saying that if they made just a Crossover book for Mage and Vampire with all the rules it would be as big or bigger than the Core book of either of the games they ran. <br /> <br /> I happen to like running something like <b>Vancouver: Dark Alliance </b>which is the bastard child setting White Wolf in the day wish it never made, where Garou and Kindred work together. I like it. It is fun to play for Vampire and Werewolf players. I have found over the years that to help the Kindred I have had to make some House Rules and changes to get the Kindred just able to even come close to being playable with their Garou Pack mates. The whole Vampire not out in the Sun thing I had to change. I had to come up with alternate rules on it (using Julian Luna and other Kindred from Kindred the Embrace as inspiration for the rule). It works but even then the Kindred are seriously lacking. The fact they can't go to the Umbra. Handle BSDs etc like a Garou can makes the game difficult. <br /> <br /> A complete cWoD crossover game... with everything. Good luck with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T18:17:45-08:00","id":402687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games#post399097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .And more importantly what was the explanation for how they all came together? Been thinking about perhaps trying to bring the idea to my table and was hoping for some perspectives.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Nobles: the Shining Host - </i>a supplement for <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b> - provides one option: a war against the Technocracy. Assuming Winter/Gehenna/Apocalypse hadn't happened, it proposes the idea of the sidhe organizing a cross-species campaign to destroy the Technocracy, whom the sidhe blame for all the banality in the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T05:20:16-07:00","id":531871,"title":"","content":"Changeline and Wraith are probably the hardest to bring together, as the Deadlands and the Dreaming are the hardest barriers to cross. Pretty much anything else can work, as long as the ST is conscious of what the players can do. (And Wraith can come in via Risen, KotE, or Mediums/Necromancers.)<br /> <br /> An 'End of the World' setting can make it easier as those barriers start to degrade, and also wide and varied enough threats, and powerful enough to require working together. (The physically tougher holding a line while the mystics perform a ritual of some sort as one example.)<br /> <br /> One of the issues with later 2nd Edition and 'Revised' was that a few developers were under the assumption that gamers running a crossover were 'doing it wrong'. But in the end, if you and your players are all having fun... you aren't doing it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T05:37:38-07:00","id":531880,"title":"","content":"Poor Mummy =p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T10:59:27-07:00","id":532070,"title":"","content":"I find running a crossover game with the Ascension Cosmology to be the best option as consensual reality allows all of the different cosmologies to fit in somewhere. there are a few issues I've come across though.<br /> <br /> Mage magick isn't really OP when you take a few things into account. first in order to be really OP they need time. not the Time Sphere just good old standard linear time. Even with rotes a mage caught flatfooted is better off running. Second in order to affect other critters at full strength you require certain prerequisites. Spirit 3 Life 3 for werewolves, Matter 3 Life 3 for vampires, Spirit 3 Entropy 4 for wraiths. I do usually change that to Entropy 3 though. I also have a house rule that requires Life 3 Prime 3 for changelings, as they are effectively living magic. and of course, just hitting them over the head with Paradox is usually enough to give any Mage pause before doing something too big.<br /> <br /> Werewolves can be a bit much at first and getting the player to operate with the others is kind of difficult in game as they specifically hate vampires and have no love of mages. but that isn't going to be a major problem.<br /> <br /> Vampires vulnerability to sunlight is another hurdle, I do allow magical items that allow them to nullify that just for convenience sake and i don't find it too unbalancing. I do stress the rule that their die pool are capped by their humanity during daylight hours and their need to feed however.<br /> <br /> Wraiths are difficult but not impossible. Werewolves and mages and vampires all have powers that allow them to see Wraiths and I stress that the Wraith player should take Arcanoi that allows them to interact with the skin lands because none of the others are going to go anywhere near the Shadow lands with out lots of precautions. It should be noted that Wraith is the game I'm least familiar with my troupe just dosn't mess with them so I've been given a pass on them so far.<br /> <br /> Changelins I've had to tweak a little just so they can keep up. Mostly I've had to make Glamour much easier to get but and lower the standard banality of to around 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T19:55:15-07:00","id":532699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games?p=532070#post532070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find running a crossover game with the Ascension Cosmology to be the best option as consensual reality allows all of the different cosmologies to fit in somewhere. there are a few issues I've come across though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only by heavily compromising their themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T04:55:10-07:00","id":533037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games?p=532699#post532699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only by heavily compromising their themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats an opinion i personally dont share, but if you are heavily invested in one splat over the other, i can see how you'd come to that conclusion. Probably for the best one avoids splat crossover in that case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T12:56:50-07:00","id":533556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games?p=533037#post533037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats an opinion i personally dont share, but if you are heavily invested in one splat over the other, i can see how you'd come to that conclusion. Probably for the best one avoids splat crossover in that case.</div> </div> </div> </div>The post was specifically about jamming everything into Mage. Which is being invested in one game over the others - Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T19:20:30-07:00","id":533897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games?p=531880#post531880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poor Mummy =p</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, mummies <i>are</i> interesting characters. No doubt about that. And they can make for cool antagonists, particularly in a campaign that spans centuries. Heck, in such a campaign, they can even (occasionally) be allies - memory can be so unreliable, even for immortals. <br /> <br /> But having them in a mixed PC party . . . that can get messy. A lot of their (physical) power is tied up in their immortality - in the fact that while they <i>can</i> die, they don't stay dead. They don't get super strength or speed, they can't shape shift, and they heal human-slow. Balancing that in combat is . . . tough<br /> <br /> Even while dead, and wandering the Underworld . . its still an issue. Mummies don't have Passions, nor do they learn Arcanoi. And their Ba (wraith-like form) can't enter the Shadowlands. So again, combat gets tricky - as does hanging out with their still-living colleagues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T11:16:07-07:00","id":535741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games?p=533556#post533556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The post was specifically about jamming everything into Mage. Which is being invested in one game over the others - Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again i must disagree, if your running a multisplat game you need to establish a common framework everything hooks onto so everyone can play together. Mage, with its basic setting idea that multiple contradictory truths have validity, or even parts of Demon, where reality exists at multiple levels and only some of it is perceived by any one group at any one time, is a better fit for a &quot;somewhat coherent&quot; shared setting.<br /> <br /> The WtA and VtM cosmologies very definitely shut down the idea anyone else knows whats going on, and very emphatically shut down any alternate explanations. Mage is more accommodating, though that comes at the price of having to posit that no-one , not the vaunted Garou or the Fallen or even the Magi really know whats going on. Players and ST are then free to use as much of the respective &quot;truths&quot; as applies to the game and ignore the rest where it adds unnecessary conflict. Though i definitely do not recommend putting a Mage player in a mixed chronicle personally.<br /> <br /> The themes of particular splat are guidelines in my opinion, not hard and fast conventions. Not every Werewolf game must be a doomed battle against an invincible opponent while lamenting the mistakes of your ancestors. Not every Vampire game must be a nuanced and soulful exploration of the soul-grinding horror of the vampiric condition. Sometimes you just want to run mixed chronicle in a shared setting and tell a good story and have some fun. Sometimes you want to heavily compromise a game's theme and play against type. That doesnt make one invested in Mage in my experience, it just means its easier to confabulate a mixed CWoD setting with Mage's setting assumptions, so long as you dont set them in steel.<br /> <br /> Your Mileage May Vary, and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T11:39:22-07:00","id":535753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games?p=535741#post535741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again i must disagree, if your running a multisplat game you need to establish a common framework everything hooks onto so everyone can play together. Mage, with its basic setting idea that multiple contradictory truths have validity, or even parts of Demon, where reality exists at multiple levels and only some of it is perceived by any one group at any one time, is a better fit for a &quot;somewhat coherent&quot; shared setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until mages start talking about &quot;inherent paradox flaws&quot; of non-mages. At that point, shit starts getting boring and there's little left unscrutinized through the lens of the game chosen to be in control. It's incredibly weird for other games to have to deal with Mage's odd complex about technology, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The WtA and VtM cosmologies very definitely shut down the idea anyone else knows whats going on, and very emphatically shut down any alternate explanations. Mage is more accommodating, though that comes at the price of having to posit that no-one , not the vaunted Garou or the Fallen or even the Magi really know whats going on. Players and ST are then free to use as much of the respective &quot;truths&quot; as applies to the game and ignore the rest where it adds unnecessary conflict. Though i definitely do not recommend putting a Mage player in a mixed chronicle personally.<br /> <br /> The themes of particular splat are guidelines in my opinion, not hard and fast conventions. Not every Werewolf game must be a doomed battle against an invincible opponent while lamenting the mistakes of your ancestors. Not every Vampire game must be a nuanced and soulful exploration of the soul-grinding horror of the vampiric condition. Sometimes you just want to run mixed chronicle in a shared setting and tell a good story and have some fun. Sometimes you want to heavily compromise a game's theme and play against type. That doesnt make one invested in Mage in my experience, it just means its easier to confabulate a mixed CWoD setting with Mage's setting assumptions, so long as you dont set them in steel.<br /> <br /> Your Mileage May Vary, and all that. </div> </div> </div>You'd need to make something entirely new. Mage won't facilitate easy cohesion. It's there to facilitate Mage, and nothing else. An actual middle ground between the games would be quite a different thing from the &quot;layered realities&quot; and &quot;multiple contradictory truths&quot; models of other games, because those are too weak to really build a cohesive setting that isn't warping between different parallel universes all of the sudden. Even discounting the world views, the monsters would have much more profound effects on each other than in any single game; you'd have to rewrite massive amounts of setting around each other game to accomplish this end properly, and each game would have to give up an awful lot of itself to meshing everything together.<br /> <br /> As for what the themes of the games are, Werewolf is less about the battle being doomed than it is a desperate struggle to turn everything around. Everything that they venerate is very real and palpable, however; Rage and Gnosis are basically defined as feeling how close things are to collapsing and the fury that this existential dread engenders. It's what gives the game its heart. Don't take out the heart unless you have a functional replacement. Note that in this case, Mage is offering to transplant the heart with a crystal that pulses kind of like a heart and glows with a psychedelic light, and can't quite comprehend why it is that the glow and fact that it's a chunk of crystal that can probably move fluid isn't counted as a reason to go through with surgery sight unseen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-01-2015, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T12:36:44-07:00","id":535796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Until mages start talking about &quot;inherent paradox flaws&quot; of non-mages. At that point, shit<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/#54713780\">STARTS<img src=\"http://cdncache-a.akamaihd.net/items/it/img/arrow-10x10.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a> getting boring and there's little left unscrutinized through the lens of the game chosen to be in control. It's incredibly weird for other games to have to deal with Mage's odd complex about technology, too. </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div>sure the MAGE player characters will do that. the vampire/werewolf/changelings are going to tell them to shut up and get on with the story. when i said that using mage's cosmology is easier its because multiple truths and understandings of the universe all exist and function together IN GAME. and ultimately the 'truth' of the situation is really anybodies guess. You can have the Abrahamic orgin of vampire being as true as the Animistic origins of the Ferra and nobody is going to be anymore wrong. your argument is all based on roleplaying situations that won't necessarily come up in the game, you can run Vampires as Vampires complete with angst and damnation with out getting into the weird metaphysics of it just as easily as you can keep the Wyrm as the Wyrm. its the an animistic personification of destruction and corruption. in mage world view is reality and thats what in my opinion makes the whole thing work.<br /> <br /> You'd need to make something entirely new. Mage won't facilitate easy cohesion. It's there to facilitate Mage, and nothing else. An actual middle ground between the games would be quite a different thing from the &quot;layered realities&quot; and &quot;multiple contradictory truths&quot; models of other games, because those are too weak to really build a cohesive setting that isn't warping between different parallel universes all of the sudden. Even discounting the world views, the monsters would have much more profound effects on each other than in any single game; you'd have to rewrite massive amounts of setting around each other game to accomplish this end properly, and each game would have to give up an awful lot of itself to meshing everything together.why? mage by its nature facilitates the other game's cosmology and fluff just fine. its compatible with Changeling (the whole belief makes magic easier thing...) Werewolf (there are boat loads of animistic mages out there) and Wraith with little to no work on your part. and even ties into Vampire (House/Clan Tremere). I'd say that the different monsters have already had pretty big impact on each other. in offical cannon even. look at The Week of Nightmares. that has the Technocracy nuking an Antideluvian which incidentally opened up the Paths of Balor in Changeling. Wraith's ending along with the Week of Nightmares helped Kick up the Avatar storm and that's just a couple of examples as to how the various game lines connect and impact each other.<br /> <br /> As for what the themes of the games are, Werewolf is less about the battle being doomed than it is a desperate struggle to turn everything around. Everything that they venerate is very real and palpable, however; Rage and Gnosis are basically defined as feeling how<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/#84494446\">CLOSE<img src=\"http://cdncache-a.akamaihd.net/items/it/img/arrow-10x10.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a> things are to collapsing and the fury that this existential dread engenders. It's what gives the game its heart. Don't take out the heart unless you have a functional replacement. Note that in this case, Mage is offering to transplant the heart with a crystal that pulses kind of like a heart and glows with a psychedelic light, and can't quite comprehend why it is that the glow and fact that it's a chunk of crystal that can probably move fluid isn't counted as a reason to go through with surgery sight unseen.your not going to run a crossover game with out sacrificing some focus on one thing or another. that doesn't mean that those themes are in anyway compromised. if just means that your focusing on aspect each group's perspective over another. Werewolves want to slow (if not stop) the spread of human industrialization, more than one groupe of mages wants to do the same thing. for much the same reason. ( a lot of mages like having access to the umbra and the free flow of Quintessence). They don't even have to be for the same reasons. Neither vampires nor werewolves gain anything if the Antediluvians rise or Pentex poisons and corrupts the human population. You just have to choose which themes you want your story to be about and run the game off that. I just suggest mage's cosmology because its more accommodating toward various 'truths' than Vampire or Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T12:53:54-07:00","id":535833,"title":"","content":"I dont know Saur OpsSpecialist, i think we're talking at cross purposes here.<br /> <br /> I think crossover is doable without significant dilution of theme, you do not and i respect that opinion. I have run a crossover game with WtA elements and Shifter PC's for 2 years and neither of my Shifter PC's feel that their experience has been hampered by the mix of elements or by using a crossover cosmology. I have put an enormous amount of work into the cosmology, because i had the time to do so, and i am happy with what i achieved.<br /> <br /> So where does that leave us? Our disagreement seems insoluble. And i am happy to leave it there, i dont think i could change your mind without you being at my table, and i dont think that is possible since we are in different countries. I am happy to leave it there, for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T16:10:18-07:00","id":536037,"title":"","content":"I'd say the key to Mage is to keep it focused on street level (to keep it from getting out of hand). Something that's also pretty important is that if a mage is going to be hanging out with a bunch of not-other-mages, those other characters are really going to make that mage think more in their terms than a traditional Mage game mage would. There are both advantages and disadvantages to that. A lot of conflicting Absolute Truths is probably going to severely hamper the mage's enlightenment, but at the same time it's probably going to give them access to a lot of things that no other mage can have or know and if they can handle it and endure, the pay-off will likely put them way ahead of most other mages who have not had that very uncommon set of experiences and revelations from the other player's characters.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could kind of mess around a bit with the idea of just who might cause Paradox. There are plenty of reasons why every other creature would cause some issues when they see the mage do something and then say &quot;WTF!!! I don't believe it!!!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T19:35:57-07:00","id":536398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games?p=535753#post535753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Until mages start talking about &quot;inherent paradox flaws&quot; of non-mages. At that point, shit starts getting boring and there's little left unscrutinized through the lens of the game chosen to be in control. It's incredibly weird for other games to have to deal with Mage's odd complex about technology, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technology = evil (- token splat) was pretty prevalent in all the lines...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T10:10:26-07:00","id":537173,"title":"","content":"Not so much in Vampire. There, the default setting for the protagonists is cities of the industrialized First World, and technology is used both by the vampire puppet-masters and the rank and file of humanity that they're hiding from in plain sight. Most of their principal antagonists (the Sabbat, the Inquisition, lupines) in some way reject modern society, whether it be through silent predation in urban blights, relying on Medieval religion and worldviews, or isolationism from civilization entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T10:55:21-07:00","id":537213,"title":"","content":"Really, the evil technology thing was just for Mage and Werewolf. Maybe a little bit in Changeling. In Vampire, technology was just what it is in real life. In Wraith technology was nothing special. The same goes for Demon, Hunter, Mummy, and... are there others?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T02:35:20-07:00","id":537940,"title":"","content":"Actually Technology isn't inherently evil in Mage or Werewolf. It was fixed in Mage by making the Technocracy point of view clear in GttT, and Werewolf doesn't have issues with Technology, it has issues with humanity's rampant abuse of nature and certain technological spirits being utterly insane and wanting to stop all reality from ever changing again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T08:47:15-07:00","id":538423,"title":"","content":"A Malkavian, a Glass Walker, an Etherite and a Knocker all walk into a bar......all the lights explode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T12:21:30-07:00","id":538674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games?p=535833#post535833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont know Saur OpsSpecialist, i think we're talking at cross purposes here.<br /> <br /> I think crossover is doable without significant dilution of theme, you do not and i respect that opinion. I have run a crossover game with WtA elements and Shifter PC's for 2 years and neither of my Shifter PC's feel that their experience has been hampered by the mix of elements or by using a crossover cosmology. I have put an enormous amount of work into the cosmology, because i had the time to do so, and i am happy with what i achieved.<br /> <br /> So where does that leave us? Our disagreement seems insoluble. And i am happy to leave it there, i dont think i could change your mind without you being at my table, and i dont think that is possible since we are in different countries. I am happy to leave it there, for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said that crossover that doesn't dilute themes would be very different from stuffing all of the other games through Mage, which would fundamentally overwhelm all things with Mage. There's a bit of difference between that and not saying it would work at all. It's really difficult to really engage with Werewolf if the setting conceits of Mage are true and humans are the most important things in the universe, and accordingly, Mage doesn't do well if humans aren't special but put themselves on an undeserved pedestal while aiding in the slow descent of the universe into corruption in the process. You're going to have to come up with something new to join them together. It's probably possible, but not with the material as it's written in any single game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T12:24:05-07:00","id":538675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games?p=536398#post536398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technology = evil (- token splat) was pretty prevalent in all the lines...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage's odd complex about technology, as I referred to it, is that it labels it another form of magic. No other game does this. Toasters are meaningfully and essentially different from using mystical power to heat up bread in any fashion you might choose. In fact, other mystic methods are meaningfully and essentially different from each other in this regard as well. Sphere theory, in general, doesn't really mesh well with other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T22:24:32-07:00","id":539234,"title":"","content":"I don't about you guys, but I would just love a game where a Fallen, a Garou and a Mage just sit down and have a philosophical discussion about their conflicting cosmology.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure it would would end with two of the players dead though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T00:12:21-07:00","id":539325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games?p=539234#post539234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't about you guys, but I would just love a game where a Fallen, a Garou and a Mage just sit down and have a philosophical discussion about their conflicting cosmology.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure it would would end with two of the players dead though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And the characters probably wouldn't fare very well, either, come to think of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T07:38:45-07:00","id":539516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games?p=539234#post539234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't about you guys, but I would just love a game where a Fallen, a Garou and a Mage just sit down and have a philosophical discussion about their conflicting cosmology.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure it would would end with two of the players dead though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Been there, done that, though it was a Changeling, Garou and Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T12:13:31-07:00","id":541554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/399097-big-five-crossover-games?p=539325#post539325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the characters probably wouldn't fare very well, either, come to think of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, no, the characters would be fine. They at least have the benefit of having supernatural powers to stop them from getting killed when arguments about WOD cosmology get heated.<br /> <br /> Ever seen a man forced to shallow ten miniatures and an entire gamebook? It's not pretty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}